---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Clarity" description="You're selling features, not solutions. Let's flip that.">
  <section class="hero-small">
    <span class="tenet-label">Core Tenet</span>
    <h1>"Our product is great but <span class="highlight">nobody gets it</span>"</h1>
    <p class="hero-answer">You're selling features, not solutions. Let's flip that.</p>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The Problem</h2>
    <div class="problem-text">
      <p>
        Your team can explain your product in 47 different ways. None of them are simple.
        You've got feature matrices, capability decks, and comparison charts — but clients still don't understand why they need you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Complex doesn't have to mean complicated. The most valuable things can be explained simply.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">How I Help</h2>
    <div class="approach">
      <div class="approach-item">
        <h3>Find the Essence</h3>
        <p>Strip away the jargon. Find the one thing you really do for clients. Make it impossible to misunderstand.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="approach-item">
        <h3>Create Depth Layers</h3>
        <p>Not everyone needs the same level of detail. I create skim/read/audit layers so executives get the headline and analysts get the proof.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="approach-item">
        <h3>Test for Clarity</h3>
        <p>If your mother can't explain it, it's not clear enough. I test messaging until it's stupidly obvious.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">Related Work</h2>
    <div class="related-work">
      <a href="/work#the-stack" class="work-link">
        <span class="work-title">The Stack</span>
        <span class="work-desc">70 pages → 3 depth layers</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/work#freed-reads" class="work-link">
        <span class="work-title">Freed Reads</span>
        <span class="work-desc">Making public domain books accessible</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section cta-section">
    <h2>Ready to simplify?</h2>
    <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com" class="cta-button">Let's Talk</a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-small {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  
  .tenet-label {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .hero-small h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  
  .hero-answer {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  
  .problem-text p {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  
  .approach {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  
  .approach-item {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: #111;
  }
  
  .approach-item h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .approach-item p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .related-work {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  
  .work-link {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #111;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }
  
  .work-link:hover {
    border-left-color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .work-title {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  
  .work-desc {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  
  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
  }
  
  .cta-section h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
